# Elasticsearch 8.15.3 with analysis-icu, for CMS complaint search in 13 languages.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# The stock elasticsearch image does not ship analysis-icu. The complaint mapping declares two
# custom analyzers, cms_indic and cms_urdu, and both are built on icu_tokenizer + icu_folding
# because Elasticsearch has NO built-in analyzer for 9 of the 13 languages this system serves:
# tamil, telugu, marathi, gujarati, kannada, malayalam, punjabi, oriya and assamese (only english,
# hindi, bengali, persian and arabic exist as built-ins). Without the plugin, creating the index
# fails outright with "Unknown tokenizer type [icu_tokenizer]" and there is no Indic search at all.
#
# VERSIONS
#   base image     docker.elastic.co/elasticsearch/elasticsearch:8.15.3
#   plugin         analysis-icu 8.15.3  (version is implicit: elasticsearch-plugin resolves the
#                                        plugin to the exact version of the node installing it, and
#                                        refuses a mismatch, so it cannot silently drift)
#   java client    8.15.5 via the Spring Boot 3.4.1 BOM — wire-compatible with an 8.15.3 server
#
# LICENCE
# The 8.15.3 distribution is Elastic License 2.0 and self-starts a Basic licence. analysis-icu does
# not appear in Elastic's licence-gating table, so it is available at Basic. Nothing the complaint
# mapping uses requires a paid tier.
FROM docker.elastic.co/elasticsearch/elasticsearch:8.15.3

# --batch accepts the plugin's security policy prompts non-interactively; without it the build
# blocks forever waiting on stdin that a docker build does not have.
RUN bin/elasticsearch-plugin install --batch analysis-icu

# Fail the BUILD, not the first request, if the plugin did not actually land.
RUN bin/elasticsearch-plugin list | grep -q analysis-icu
